{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And they shall shepherd</b> — by way of parable, for they shall rule over you by force." "<b>And the land of Nimrod</b> — it is Babylon." "<b>At its entrances</b> — concerning the sword, like 'and they are openings.' Some say: at the entrances of the land, and behold they shall deliver from Assyria."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {2 "Ibn Ezra quotes the phrase והמה פתיחות (Ezekiel 41:16) as a parallel for the sense of פתח as an architectural opening; the second opinion takes 'entrances' geographically."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:06.514528069Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}